  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nUnseasonable warmth will continue through Tuesday, and humidity\nlevels will also be on the rise early next week. South winds will\nstrengthen Sunday into early next week, which will raise fire\nweather concerns for a couple days before humidity levels show a\nmore significant rise by Tuesday.\n\nSouthwest flow aloft and an approaching cold front will result in\nincreasing shower and thunderstorm chances late Tuesday through\nThursday. The GFS continues to bring a stronger upper system out\nof the southwest U.S. into the plains which would suggest some\nsevere weather threat in our area, but both the ECMWF and UKMET\nhold the main upper system back west, which would limit the severe\nweather threat. Either way, a surface cold front moves through the\narea by late week bringing cooler temperatures, although the\neventual evolution of the upper trough will dictate whether we see\nsome cool fall mornings for a change by next weekend.",
